<urn:atm:triage:finding/ARCH-AY-R2-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ARCH-AY-R2-003" ;
  triage:title "undocumented third HerdrEndpointDoctor test-double impl site missing from boundary TOML allowlist" ;
  triage:description "arch-qa quality-gate-r3 verification (PR #1318 fix/ay-gate-r2-schema-docs, head ef79745ae56aaeb62e6f70a91cf4acad2360ee5c). Important. RULE-012 boundary enforcement requires all test-double implementation sites outside the primary crate to be explicitly listed in the boundary TOML's allowed_test_double_paths. boundaries/atm-core/herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml [testing].allowed_test_double_paths is currently empty (`= []`). However, crates/atm-runtime/src/doctor_projection.rs:384 contains `impl HerdrEndpointDoctor for CountingEndpoint`, a test-double implementation site inside a #[cfg(test)] mod tests block. Per RULE-012, impl sites outside the boundary's allowlist are findings regardless of #[cfg(test)] gating. The impl and boundary record predate phase-ay; the boundary file was created net-new in this phase without documenting this legitimate test-double site. Required correction: add the actual qualified path of CountingEndpoint (likely `atm_runtime::doctor_projection::testing::CountingEndpoint` or equivalent) to herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml's [testing].allowed_test_double_paths, since this is a legitimate test double that simply was not documented when the boundary record was created." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "RULE-012 boundary allowlist" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-08T04:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-08T05:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Confirmed fixed by arch-ctm on PR #1320 (fix/ay-gate-r3-arch, 170ae2dffe4a86f4cb873de76bea8352c2d55352). Independently re-verified by quality-mgr via direct file reads plus a live fmt/clippy/test run (not taken on arch-ctm's fix notice alone). herdr-endpoint-doctor.toml's [testing].allowed_test_double_paths now lists both actual impl sites: crate::doctor::ClosedHerdrEndpointDoctor (production, doctor/mod.rs:58) and atm_runtime::doctor_projection::tests::CountingEndpoint (test double, doctor_projection.rs:384). No unauthorized impl site remains." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-08T04:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ARCH-AY-R2-003/ARCH-AY-R2-003/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ARCH-AY-R2-003/ARCH-AY-R2-003/2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

